- op: discuss  # a067
  at: '2026-09-16T00:59:16Z'  # a067
  by: agent  # a067
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a067
  clock: 6  # a067
  nonce: a067  # a067
  message: "DONE in PR #979, merged to dev at 20f03bf9ae. Owner approved implementation and\nauto-pr without --gov.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-run on merged dev rather than on the branch:\n  ./scripts/ci-debug pr-body 922   -> exit 0, \"Body:   present\", the full\n  markdown description fenced. That is the item's own filed repro -- the\n  question that opened this (\"can you see the PR message for PR 922?\") and\n  could not be answered before.\n  ./scripts/ci-debug pr-body 979   -> exit 0, this PR's own body.\n  ./scripts/ci-debug pr-body 999999 -> exit 1, \"Failed to fetch PR #999999\n  (HTTP 404)\" -- a missing PR stays distinguishable from a missing body.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED\n  * json_text_state in scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh: present | empty | null |\n    absent | other | unreadable. json_bool_state's sibling for strings, for\n    the same recorded reason -- json_field renders a JSON null, an absent key\n    and a parse failure identically as the empty string.\n  * cmd_pr_body in scripts/ci-debug, plus usage and dispatch. One API call,\n    the one pr-status already made; pinned by a test so a future second call\n    breaks it.\n  * Output fenced under a per-invocation nonce, because a PR body is\n    author-controlled text and the consumer is an agent.\n\nDESIGN POINT 1 SURVIVED CONTACT, WITH A CORRECTION. The unreadable arm was\nnearly decorative: my first test fed an HTML error page and FAILED, because\napi_call shape-checks the first byte and returns 2 before the reader sees\nanything. The arm is reachable by two other shapes, both now tested -- a\ntruncated payload starting with a brace, and an HTTP 200 carrying zero bytes,\nwhich is WI-holik's exact defect against a different endpoint. Had I not run\nthe test I would have shipped an unreachable branch and a test that proved\nnothing.\n\nTESTS: 11 new in tests/test_ci_debug_github.py, including a negative control\nthat a body-less PR reports rather than errors, a three-way separability check\non empty/null/absent, and a forged-fence arm. 1795 passed in the affected\nslice; mypy ratchet clean at 669.\n\nFILED AT P3 AND NOT RE-PRICED. Priority is the owner's."  # a067
